            {"heading": "The Pattern Recognition Practice", "body": ["The most useful question in healing work is not 'what happened to me?' but 'what keeps happening?' The patterns that repeat in relationships, at work, with authority, with intimacy — these are the wound in action.", "Write down the five most consistent complaints you receive from people close to you. Then write the five most consistent ways you respond to stress in relationships. Then ask: do these patterns remind me of anything from my family of origin? The answer is usually yes.", "This isn't about blame. It's about seeing the loop clearly enough to step out of it."]},
