            {"heading": "Holding Both", "body": ["You can forgive someone — release yourself from carrying the wound — while maintaining clear limits about that person's access to you. Forgiveness does not obligate continued relationship.", "People who are unsafe — who have demonstrated through repeated behavior that they will harm you given proximity — can be forgiven at a distance. The forgiveness is internal. The boundary is relational.", "In fact, forgiving someone genuinely often becomes easier when you're no longer in contact with them — because forgiveness is no longer confused with trust, and the relationship's reality can't keep re-injuring the healing wound."]},
