            {"heading": "The Long Road", "body": ["For severe violations — abuse, assault, profound betrayal — forgiveness is often a years-long process, not a decision made in a contemplative moment. Expecting rapid forgiveness for severe wounds is both unrealistic and unkind to yourself.", "The goal is not to feel no resentment. The goal is for the resentment to have less and less hold on your daily experience over time — not because the wound was minor, but because your current life deserves your presence more than the past does.", "If you find that a significant wound is actively dominating your present experience — your relationships, your wellbeing, your capacity for joy — working with a therapist who specializes in trauma and forgiveness often accelerates this process significantly."]},
