        {"title": "Reading Other People", "intro": "Social and empathic accuracy is the interpersonal component of emotional intelligence.", "sections": [
            {"heading": "Tuning In", "body": ["Empathic accuracy is the ability to read what another person is actually feeling — not what they're saying they feel, not what you imagine you'd feel in their situation, but what they're actually experiencing.", "This skill is built through: genuine curiosity about others' inner experience, asking rather than assuming, noticing nonverbal signals (face, body, tone, pacing), and suspending your own emotional narrative long enough to actually receive theirs.", "The most common failure mode: projective empathy — feeling what you'd feel in their situation and assuming it's what they feel. This is better than no empathy but often misses the specific reality of another person's experience."]},
        ], "callout": "Empathy is listening with your whole attention, not just waiting to relate."},
