            {"heading": "The Core Distortions", "body": ["Catastrophizing: assuming the worst possible outcome is the most likely. 'My boss seemed annoyed — I'm going to be fired — I'll never find another job — I'll lose my apartment.' Each step in the chain is treated as certain when it is actually speculative.", "Probability distortion: treating low-probability events as likely because they are vivid and frightening. Flying feels more dangerous than driving because crashes are dramatic — it is statistically far safer.", "The interventions: 'What's the actual probability of the worst case?' 'What's the best case? What's the most likely case?' 'Have I survived similar situations before?' 'What would I tell a friend thinking this?'", "CBT (Cognitive Behavioral Therapy) for anxiety has the most extensive evidence base of any psychological intervention. If your anxiety is significantly impairing your life, working through CBT with a therapist or via a structured workbook is highly recommended."]},
